@page "/docs/theming/themes"

@* Setting the app's look with IzzyTheme: preset, brand, grays, radius, density, fonts. From
   docs/styling.md ("Presets and colors", "Customizing"); values checked against ThemeValues.cs. *@

<ArticlePage Section="theming" Slug="themes">
    <Lead>
        Set the whole app's look in one place: <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> in <Code>App.razor</Code>'s <Code>head</Code> takes a
        preset, then your brand color, grays, radius, density and fonts over it. It renders on the server, so the theme is
        there on first paint, with no script and in every render mode.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">Set the theme</Heading>
        <TextBlock>Put one <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> in the <Code>head</Code>, after the stylesheet:</TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor" Title="Components/App.razor">@SetTheme</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            Each setting beats the preset's own; leave it unset to take the preset's. With none at all you get the Standard
            preset in blue on neutral grays.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Presets</Heading>
        <TextBlock>Use <Code>Preset</Code> for a starting set of defaults: density, shape, type and colors that suit a kind of app.</TextBlock>
        <ExampleViewer Example="izzy-theme-presets" />
        <TextBlock>On part of a page a preset doesn't bring its brand and gray, so each card sets them too. Fonts are app-wide, so Editorial's don't show here.</TextBlock>
        <Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Preset</th><th>For</th><th>Controls</th><th>Shape</th><th>Type</th><th>Brand</th><th>Gray</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>Standard</code></td><td>Internal tools, line-of-business</td><td>36px</td><td>Medium radius, hairline shadow</td><td>Inter</td><td>Blue</td><td>Neutral</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Compact</code></td><td>Admin, ERP, finance, data grids</td><td>32px, tight rows</td><td>Small radius, borders only</td><td>Inter</td><td>Indigo</td><td>Slate</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Soft</code></td><td>Consumer apps, education, health</td><td>40px, roomy</td><td>Large radius, gentle shadow</td><td>Inter</td><td>Teal</td><td>Neutral</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>Editorial</code></td><td>Docs, publishing, knowledge bases</td><td>36px</td><td>Large radius</td><td>IBM Plex Sans, Newsreader headings</td><td>Ink</td><td>Stone</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </Prose>
        <TextBlock>Editorial's fonts aren't served with IzzyBlazor: load them yourself, as under <Anchor Href="docs/theming/themes#fonts">Fonts</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Your brand color</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Use <Code>Brand</Code> with a hex color, or the name of a built-in one. It becomes the primary accent: primary
            buttons, links, focus rings, the field halo, selected rows, switches and sliders.
        </TextBlock>
        <ExampleViewer Example="izzy-theme-brands" />
        <TextBlock>
            From a hex color IzzyBlazor works out the fill, the text on it, the color as text and a soft tint, in light and
            dark, each checked for contrast. In light mode the fill is your color, unless no text can reach 4.5:1 on it; then
            only its lightness moves. In dark mode a dark color is lifted so controls still show. To set the shades yourself, see
            <Anchor Href="docs/theming/tokens#brand-shades-by-hand">Brand shades by hand</Anchor>.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Grays</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Use <Code>Gray</Code> with <Code>neutral</Code> (the default), <Code>slate</Code> (cool) or <Code>stone</Code>
            (warm, for serif headings), or a hex color for your light page. From a hex color the surfaces, fills, borders and
            text are worked out in its hue, with the text checked for contrast and a dark set to match. A very light or dark
            page color is kept light enough for text to read.
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@Grays</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Radius and density</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Use <Code>Radius</Code> to round everything in proportion: <Code>None</Code>, <Code>Sm</Code>, <Code>Md</Code> (the
            default), <Code>Lg</Code>, or <Code>Full</Code> for pill-shaped controls. Use <Code>Density</Code> for control
            heights, table rows and card padding: <Code>Compact</Code> (32px), <Code>Standard</Code> (36px) or
            <Code>Comfortable</Code> (40px).
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Fonts</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Body text is Inter, served with IzzyBlazor: browsers download only the character sets a page uses, and nothing
            once you name another font. Use <Code>BodyFont</Code>, <Code>HeadingFont</Code> and <Code>MonoFont</Code> for your
            own fonts, and <Code>HeadingWeight</Code> for the headings' weight. Load any font other than Inter yourself:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@Fonts</Code>
        <TextBlock>The Editorial preset uses IBM Plex Sans and Newsreader:</TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@EditorialFonts</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">App-wide or part of a page</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Fonts, <Code>HeadingWeight</Code>, a hex <Code>Gray</Code> and <Code>Scrollbars</Code> (whether the page's own
            scrollbar is themed too) are app-wide: set them on the <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> in the <Code>head</Code>. The rest
            also work on part of a page; see <Anchor Href="docs/theming/tokens#theme-part-of-a-page">Theme part of a page</Anchor>.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            For a strict Content-Security-Policy, pass your nonce as <Code>Nonce</Code>: hex colors and fonts come in a small
            <Code>style</Code> block.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Next steps</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/theming/color-scheme">Light and dark</Anchor>: the default scheme and a switch for readers.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/theming/tokens">Tokens and customizing</Anchor>: exact values with CSS variables.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/izzy-theme/api">IzzyTheme API</Anchor>: every parameter.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private const string SetTheme = """
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["_content/IzzyBlazor.Core/izzyblazor.css"]" />
        <IzzyTheme Preset="ThemePreset.Soft" Brand="#0a7d5a" Radius="ThemeRadius.Full" />
        """;

    private const string Grays = """
        <IzzyTheme Gray="slate" />
        @* or your light page color; app-wide *@
        <IzzyTheme Gray="#f4efe6" />
        """;

    private const string EditorialFonts = """
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=Newsreader:opsz,wght@6..72,500..600&display=swap" />
        """;

    private const string Fonts = """
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Sora:wght@400;600;700&display=swap" />
        <IzzyTheme BodyFont="Sora, system-ui, sans-serif" HeadingWeight="700" />
        """;
}
